This implementation is derived from AMD's MLPerf Training v5.1 llama2_70b_lora implementation (MI300X), as
published in the MLPerf Training v5.1 results and shipped in the container rocm/amd-mlperf:llama2_70b_training_5.1
at /workspace/code (its README is README_upstream_AMD_v5.1.md). Files carrying "Copyright (c) 2024, NVIDIA
CORPORATION" headers are licensed by NVIDIA under the Apache License, Version 2.0; their headers are retained. Files
not listed below are AMD's, unchanged (AMD's own Dockerfile and its configs for other GPUs are not included).

Files modified by Krai Ltd (no notice is added inside src/train.py and src/callbacks/custom_callbacks.py, so that
line numbers in the MLPerf result logs match this code):
  config_MI300X_1x8x1.sh (a block appended at the end), src/train.py, src/callbacks/custom_callbacks.py,
  src/conf/megatron_gpt_peft_tuning_config.yaml
Files added by Krai Ltd: Dockerfile (builds the image), patches/ (patch modules, their checks and tests, and
te_algos_fix7.csv, a hipBLASLt algorithm selection read by Transformer Engine via TE_HIPBLASLT_ALGO_LOAD; data, no
code), te_patches/, README.md, README_kernel_changes.md. patches/hs_*.py, te_algos_fix7.csv, check_swiglu_exact.py
and test_hs_*.py, lora_dropout_packed.py, eval_trim.py and the
check_lora_*.py and check_eval_trim*.py checks were written by Krai Ltd.

te_patches/linear.py and te_patches/layernorm_linear.py are Transformer Engine 2.2 (ROCm) files from that container
(Apache License, Version 2.0), with one line changed each; the Dockerfile copies them over the installed ones.

